*Difference between Agile & DevOps:

 
🔥 Agile Builds It. DevOps Runs It.
Agile focuses on how software is built.
DevOps focuses on how software is delivered and run.
⚡ Agile
Emphasizes planning, coding, and testing
Works in short sprints
Goal: Faster development & better collaboration
🔁 DevOps
Extends Agile beyond development
Focuses on CI/CD, automation, monitoring
Goal: Faster, reliable, continuous delivery
🎯 Key Difference
Agile ends at “Done”.
DevOps starts at “Done” and continues to production.
💡 Best practice:
Agile + DevOps together = Fast development + Stable releases





