✔ Runs containers on a single host
✔ Perfect for development & small setups

👉 Think of Docker as:

“Run my application inside a container”
☸️ Kubernetes (Container Orchestration Platform)
Kubernetes manages many containers at scale.

What Kubernetes does:
✔ Runs containers across multiple machines (nodes)
✔ Automatically handles scaling & self-healing
✔ Manages pods, services, and networking
✔ Best for production environments

👉 Think of Kubernetes as:
“Manage thousands of containers automatically”

🔁 How They Work Together
 • Docker builds containers
 • Kubernetes runs and manages those containers
They are not competitors — they work together.

