*HTTP client errors:

1. HTTP Error Codes (Frontend, Backend, API, ALB, Nginx, Apache)

1xx – Informational
* 100 Continue → Client continues sending request (normal handshake).
* 101 Switching Protocols → WebSockets / HTTP2 upgrade happening.

2xx – Success
* 200 OK → Request successful.
* 201 Created → Resource created (POST).
* 204 No Content → Successful but no body returned.

3xx – Redirect
* 301 Moved Permanently → URL changed.
* 302 Found → Temporary redirect.
* 304 Not Modified → Cached response.

4xx – Client Errors
* 400 Bad Request → Invalid request body, JSON wrong, missing headers.
* 401 Unauthorized → No valid auth token.
* 403 Forbidden → Access denied (IAM/API permissions or roles missing).
* 404 Not Found → URL/route incorrect.
* 405 Method Not Allowed → Wrong HTTP method (GET vs POST).
* 408 Timeout → Client too slow.
* 409 Conflict → Duplicate resource or version conflict.
* 413 Payload Too Large → Upload body too big.
* 429 Too Many Requests → Rate limit exceeded or throttling.

5xx – Server Errors
* 500 Internal Server Error → App crashed, bug in backend.
* 501 Not Implemented → Feature not handled.
* 502 Bad Gateway → ALB/Nginx got invalid response from backend.
* 503 Service Unavailable → Service down or target group empty.
* 504 Gateway Timeout → Backend taking too long or network blocked.

AWS LOAD BALANCER (ALB/ELB) Errors
* Target.FailedHealthChecks → App /health endpoint failing.
* 502 – Bad Gateway → App crashed or wrong protocol.
* 503 – No healthy targets → Target group empty.
* 504 – Timeout → Backend slow.
